# The compositor.
#
# IT RUNS BESIDE THE CONSOLE, NOT INSTEAD OF IT, AND THAT IS THE IMPORTANT
# DECISION. STAGE5.md describes `exec labwc` from /etc/profile, which would
# replace the login shell -- and a compositor that exits then leaves a machine
# with no shell at all. This one WILL exit, repeatedly, while it is being
# brought up: no DRM device, no seat, a broken rc.xml. The serial console has
# to stay the thing that always works, so labwc is its own service and the
# getty keeps running.
#
# restart = false FOR THE SAME REASON. dinit would otherwise respawn a
# compositor that cannot start, once per second, filling the console with the
# same error and hiding the boot. One attempt, one message, and `dinitctl start
# labwc` to try again after fixing something.
#
# WHAT IT DEPENDS ON, and each is a real failure this ordering prevents:
#   seatd         no session, no DRM device
#   xdg-runtime   labwc exits at src/main.c:242 if XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset
#   early-filesystems  /run must be a tmpfs before either of the above
#
# THE ENVIRONMENT IS SET HERE AND NOT INHERITED. dinit does not source
# /etc/profile -- that is a login shell's job -- so a service started at boot
# gets PID 1's environment, which has neither XDG_RUNTIME_DIR nor a usable
# PATH. The wrapper script sets both.
#
# IN boot.d NOW, AND THE NOTE THAT SAID OTHERWISE IS WORTH KEEPING IN VIEW.
# It read: "Adding the symlink would start a compositor on every boot,
# including the harness boots that exist to run package tests, and a failure
# there would look like a broken system rather than a machine with no display.
# Start it with `dinitctl start labwc`, or add the symlink once the session is
# known to work."
#
# BOTH OF ITS CONDITIONS ARE NOW MET. A harness boot never reaches dinit at
# all -- guest/init runs the suite under the default `veron.boot=test` and
# powers off, and only `veron.boot=system` switch_roots -- so nothing here can
# be reached by a package test. And the session is known to work: it has been
# started by hand on a laptop, repeatedly, since.
#
# THE FALLBACK IS WHAT MAKES IT SAFE, and it is the paragraph above rather
# than anything added here. restart = false plus a console service that runs
# independently means a compositor that cannot start costs one error message
# and leaves a shell.
type = process
command = /bin/busybox sh /etc/dinit.d/scripts/labwc-session
restart = false

# logfile SO A FAILURE SAYS WHY. labwc terminated with exit code 1 on the boot
# of run 85938164747 and started fine from dinitctl a moment later; the console
# carried dinit's report of the exit but not a word from labwc itself, because
# its stderr went into the same serial stream as everything else and did not
# survive. With this the reason lands in a file the desktop test can read back.
logfile = /run/labwc.log
depends-on = seatd
depends-on = xdg-runtime
depends-on = early-filesystems
